<%
  /* Shared partial (WI #273 / R2 + R3, finding F8): the data-security-controls block.
     Before this it was copy-pasted between sad.md.tmpl and as-built.md.tmpl and had
     DRIFTED in both wording and heading level:
       - sad:      `## Security concerns` (under `# Security`) + `## Security control
                   inheritance and dependencies`, controls behind a bare `<% if %>`.
       - as-built: `# Data security controls` (own top-level section) + `## Inheritance
                   and dependencies`, controls already via `na()`.
     The heading *text* and *level* genuinely differ because the parent context differs
     (sad nests it inside its Security view; as-built gives it its own section), and
     unifying them would change the populated render — which WI #273's hard constraint
     forbids. So the caller passes the two heading strings; the partial owns the shared
     structure. R3: `controls` is a required field in both artefacts' `requires`, so its
     heading now always renders via `na()`, never a bare `<% if %>`.
     Caller passes { dsc, controlsHeading, inheritanceHeading }. */
%>
<%~ it.controlsHeading %>

<%~ na(it.dsc.controls) %>
<% if (it.dsc['inheritance-and-dependencies']) { %>
<%~ it.inheritanceHeading %>

<%~ it.dsc['inheritance-and-dependencies'] %>
<% } %>
